WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Gas prices hit $4.48 a gallon, up 17 cents in a week, pressuring Canadian transport holdings. This is Modern Investing Techniques, episode 179. Quick reminder, everything we discuss here is for education and entertainment. The practice investment of the day uses simulated trades with no real money. I'm not a licensed financial advisor, and this isn't financial advice. Always do your own research before putting real money to work. The TSX rose over

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:38.580
200 points led by technology stocks. The NASDAQ composite closed at 27,244, with a year-to-date

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:46.440
gain of 17.25%. New research shows the timing of Fed rate moves has shifted away from FOMC

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:53.660
meetings toward intermeeting data releases. Options flow turned sharply bullish with $674 million

00:00:53.660 --> 00:01:01.400
dollars in call purchases against 184 million in puts. Diesel prices rose 76% year over

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:08.180
year according to triple A data. The S&amp;P 500 showed mixed action while Canadian equities benefited

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:14.000
from sector rotation into technology names. Market participants are watching how intermeeting

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.900
communications from the Fed may influence rate path expectations in the weeks ahead.

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:24.500
A volume confirmation filter requires checking whether a stock's trading volume exceeds its

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:27.660
20-day average before entering a position on news.

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:34.360
Today's options data shows 3-to-1 bullish flow concentrated in index products which often

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:37.840
precedes broad market moves rather than single-name breakouts.

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:43.160
To implement this, Canadian investors can pull volume statistics from their brokerage

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:48.260
platform or a free screener and compare the current session to the 20-day line before

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:50.560
for committing capital in a TFSA.

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:54.860
The approach worked best during the 2023 rate hiking cycle

00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:57.560
when low volume rallies frequently reversed

00:01:57.560 --> 00:01:58.620
within two sessions.

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:02.420
Risks include missing fast moves in low float names

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:04.320
where volume spikes lay in the day.

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:06.820
Pair the filter with the existing rule

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:08.760
that already requires volume above

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:11.000
the 20-day average on catalyst entries.

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:15.040
Investors should also note that index-heavy options activity

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:17.180
can mask weaker single-name conviction.

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:22.740
The filter helps avoid entries where headline optimism lacks supporting participation from

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:23.500
market makers.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:28.660
Imagine you bought a Canadian bank stock last quarter after it reported steady dividend

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:31.420
growth and you plan to hold for the yield alone.

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:36.640
The order filled at the prevailing price, but the real mechanics involve understanding how

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:41.900
Buffett evolved from buying cheap assets to owning high-quality businesses with durable

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:43.180
competitive advantages.

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:49.520
His early gram style focused on cigar vat stocks trading below liquidation value, while

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:55.060
Munger pushed him toward compounders with economic modes such as brand strength or network effects.

00:02:55.540 --> 00:03:00.920
Key principles include staying inside a circle of competence, demanding a margin of safety

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:06.120
on every purchase, and recognizing that most investors are better off with low-cost index

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:07.920
funds rather than stock picking.

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:14.180
Notable holdings like Coca-Cola demonstrated the power of predictable free cash flow over decades,

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:19.040
while mistakes such as the initial Solomon Brothers investment showed the cost of ignoring

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:25.340
management quality. Modern DIY investors can apply the same checklist by screening for companies

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:31.840
with consistent return on equity above 15% and debt levels below industry averages before adding

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:34.280
to a TFSA or RRSP.

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:40.080
The misconception to avoid is treating every cheap stock as a bargain, without first confirming

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:42.480
the business can compound earnings over time.

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:47.820
Buffet's evolution highlights the value of patience in allowing quality businesses to

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:51.540
deliver returns through retained earnings rather than frequent trading.

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:57.540
Canadian investors can mirror this by focusing on companies with wide modes in regulated sectors

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:02.260
like banking or utilities, where competitive positions remain stable over decades.

